04:22.000 --> 04:30.000
Now I'm going to, because the edge here that is estimated is subjected to the noisy observation,

04:30.000 --> 04:40.000
this means that the transfer of xi to the image of xi prime via H over here is not going to be transferred exactly.

04:40.000 --> 04:46.000
This means that the transferred point of xi is not going to coincide exactly with xi prime here,

04:46.000 --> 04:50.000
because H is computed using noisy measurements.

04:50.000 --> 04:54.000
So now suppose that the transfer leads to this point over here,

04:54.000 --> 05:02.000
this point here, which I'm going to call H xi, because it's the transferred point using H and xi over here,

05:02.000 --> 05:12.000
there is going to be a certain discrepancy between the observed point of xi and xi prime after the transformation.

05:12.000 --> 05:16.000
Hence, we are going to compute this distance here as such,

05:16.000 --> 05:23.000
the Euclidean distance between the xi prime and the transferred point of xi via the homography of H.

05:23.000 --> 05:27.000
And we'll use this as the transfer error.

05:27.000 --> 05:31.000
So this is the Euclidean image distance in the second image,

05:31.000 --> 05:38.000
between the measured point xi and the corresponding point H of xi that's transferred from the first point.

05:38.000 --> 05:43.000
And we'll use this error to estimate the homography.

05:43.000 --> 05:51.000
This means that we want to estimate a homography such that the error between the original point that is observed xi prime

05:51.000 --> 05:56.000
and the transferred point of H xi is minimised.

05:56.000 --> 06:05.000
So in the previous slide, we look at the error that is incurred within one image when the point from the other image xi

06:05.000 --> 06:12.000
is being transferred to the second image here xi prime via H here.

06:12.000 --> 06:15.000
This is a one sided or one image error transfer.

06:15.000 --> 06:23.000
Now, it makes more sense that we are minimising the error from both sides of the transfer.

06:23.000 --> 06:26.000
Hence, we call this the symmetric transfer error,

06:26.000 --> 06:36.000
where instead of just transferring the error or transferring the point from xi image 1 to image 2 over here via H

06:36.000 --> 06:41.000
